1
00:00:39,125 --> 00:00:41,791
Well, that settles it.

2
00:00:41,792 --> 00:00:44,459
That you are not the culprit.

3
00:00:49,417 --> 00:00:50,499
Well...

4
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:53,583
Anyway, what should we do?
The car is all burned up.

5
00:00:53,584 --> 00:00:56,291
Now we have no way of proving the car was hacked.

6
00:00:56,292 --> 00:00:58,416
Actually, we can.

7
00:00:58,417 --> 00:01:02,917
I regularly upload the vehicle data
to a backup cloud server.

8
00:01:02,918 --> 00:01:06,625
At first, I only uploaded driving logs
and test driving records.

9
00:01:06,626 --> 00:01:10,499
After the accident,
I added battery status, comm logs,

10
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:12,499
update requests, everything.

11
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:15,292
So, you have evidence it was hacked?

12
00:01:17,542 --> 00:01:20,292
They will tell us who did this.

13
00:01:33,584 --> 00:01:35,416
Mr. Cho?

14
00:01:35,417 --> 00:01:37,041
Good to see you.

15
00:01:37,042 --> 00:01:38,958
Uh, hi.

16
00:01:38,959 --> 00:01:41,459
This is your laptop, right?

17
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:46,583
- Yes.
- Good. You brought your own evidence.

18
00:01:46,584 --> 00:01:48,541
Evidence?

19
00:01:48,542 --> 00:01:49,917
I don't understand-.

20
00:01:49,918 --> 00:01:52,958
You were so busy tailing Yoon Ji Yoon,

21
00:01:52,959 --> 00:01:56,959
you didn't notice me following you.

22
00:02:14,834 --> 00:02:16,833
That Ms. Yoon you were chasing,

23
00:02:16,834 --> 00:02:18,999
she is one thorough woman.

24
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,541
She is always prepared.

25
00:02:21,542 --> 00:02:23,833
Ms. Yoon had been storing log data

26
00:02:23,834 --> 00:02:26,666
to a backup cloud server in real time.

27
00:02:26,667 --> 00:02:28,541
Remote access records,

28
00:02:28,542 --> 00:02:30,249
battery overheating data,

29
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:33,208
time of command, IP address list,

30
00:02:33,209 --> 00:02:37,250
and even the laptop serial number.

31
00:02:39,459 --> 00:02:42,124
I don't know what you're talking about.

32
00:02:42,125 --> 00:02:44,791
Cloud log? Serial number?

33
00:02:44,792 --> 00:02:48,250
Don't you know they're easy to manipulate?

34
00:02:49,626 --> 00:02:53,042
- You are framing-
- It's all over.

35
00:02:57,250 --> 00:03:00,458
The laptop in your hand,

36
00:03:00,459 --> 00:03:04,708
it's the one used to give the command.
You know that, don't you?

37
00:03:04,709 --> 00:03:08,499
Cho Geun Won, you are under arrest
for illegal intrusion and attempted murder.

38
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:12,041
You have the right to remain silent,
and the right to an attorney,

39
00:03:12,042 --> 00:03:16,834
What you say can and will be used
against you in court.

40
00:03:18,751 --> 00:03:21,000
- Not too rough.
- Yes, ma'am.

41
00:03:30,918 --> 00:03:35,876
Cho Geun Won, what is your motive
for doing this to Yoon Ji Yoon?

42
00:03:39,709 --> 00:03:42,292
I wanted to protect it.

43
00:03:43,417 --> 00:03:44,708
The company I built.

44
00:03:44,709 --> 00:03:46,959
No, you did it to hide.

45
00:03:47,542 --> 00:03:49,500
Hide what you did.

46
00:03:53,918 --> 00:03:55,958
<i>That Baek Sung Min...</i>

47
00:03:55,959 --> 00:03:57,791
<i>All you have to do
is to make him change his mind.</i>

48
00:03:57,792 --> 00:04:00,083
<i>You can't even do that?</i>

49
00:04:03,167 --> 00:04:05,333
If you can't get the IPO,

50
00:04:05,334 --> 00:04:07,834
you are useless to me.

51
00:04:08,417 --> 00:04:12,292
When that happens, losing the company
would be least of your worries.

52
00:04:14,292 --> 00:04:16,917
Your name will be obliterated

53
00:04:16,918 --> 00:04:21,542
from both the industry and academic circles.

54
00:04:32,375 --> 00:04:34,291
This is just a beta.

55
00:04:34,292 --> 00:04:36,249
We can sort it out before release!

56
00:04:36,250 --> 00:04:40,416
You've been saying that for three months already!

57
00:04:40,417 --> 00:04:41,917
Hey.

58
00:04:41,918 --> 00:04:45,166
Don't you see how important this is?

59
00:04:45,167 --> 00:04:46,541
If we give up,

60
00:04:46,542 --> 00:04:48,750
we can kiss investments and partners goodbye!

61
00:04:48,751 --> 00:04:51,875
So we should keep doing this until someone dies?

62
00:04:51,876 --> 00:04:54,333
People's lives are at stake!

63
00:04:54,334 --> 00:04:56,374
You are betting on a 'maybe.'

64
00:04:56,375 --> 00:04:58,124
That is not science!

65
00:04:58,125 --> 00:04:59,625
It's a gamble!

66
00:04:59,626 --> 00:05:01,291
Sung Min,

67
00:05:01,292 --> 00:05:04,249
when did you become such a coward?

68
00:05:04,250 --> 00:05:06,333
Geun Won.

69
00:05:06,334 --> 00:05:09,959
This is not cowardice.
This is called responsibility.

70
00:05:11,083 --> 00:05:13,626
It's you who lost your way.

71
00:05:26,959 --> 00:05:29,918
Sung Min wouldn't back down.

72
00:05:30,459 --> 00:05:34,291
He insisted on going public
with that beta code issue.

73
00:05:34,292 --> 00:05:37,249
He was even willing to shut the project down.

74
00:05:37,250 --> 00:05:38,666
- So-
- So you pushed ahead anyway,

75
00:05:38,667 --> 00:05:41,999
even though you knew the risks.

76
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:45,626
And tried to kill Yoon Ji Yoon
so that the world wouldn't know?

77
00:05:47,918 --> 00:05:50,124
That's why you killed Dr. Baek too?

78
00:05:50,125 --> 00:05:52,166
- To shut him up?
- No.

79
00:05:52,167 --> 00:05:53,541
I didn't kill Sung Min.

80
00:05:53,542 --> 00:05:55,917
- Mr. Cho-
- I'm not lying.

81
00:05:55,918 --> 00:05:58,333
I was out of the country.

82
00:05:58,334 --> 00:06:00,375
It's not me, for real.

83
00:06:11,918 --> 00:06:16,374
I pulled this log data
from the Chimera HQ server.

84
00:06:16,375 --> 00:06:20,750
The algorithm was planted
around midnight on April 2nd.

85
00:06:20,751 --> 00:06:23,708
My admin account was used.

86
00:06:23,709 --> 00:06:26,583
But the IP address is not from a VPN.

87
00:06:26,584 --> 00:06:28,833
It's on Chimera's internal network.

88
00:06:28,834 --> 00:06:31,875
No sign of entry from outside at that time.

89
00:06:31,876 --> 00:06:33,791
Then Cho Geun Won's alibi is...

90
00:06:33,792 --> 00:06:37,166
If Mr. Cho was out of the country,

91
00:06:37,167 --> 00:06:39,249
he couldn't have accessed it in person.

92
00:06:39,250 --> 00:06:42,082
What does this mean?
Someone from the company helped him?

93
00:06:42,083 --> 00:06:45,917
I created the admin account for research.

94
00:06:45,918 --> 00:06:49,208
I'm the only one who knows the password.

95
00:06:49,209 --> 00:06:51,541
No, there is one...

96
00:06:51,542 --> 00:06:53,583
Dr. Baek?

97
00:06:53,584 --> 00:06:56,041
- But Dr. Baek is...
- No way.

98
00:06:56,042 --> 00:06:58,333
He was the one who died in that car.

99
00:06:58,334 --> 00:07:00,583
I can't imagine him
doing that to his pregnant wife.

100
00:07:00,584 --> 00:07:01,708
No way.

101
00:07:01,709 --> 00:07:05,751
If it's neither Cho Geun Won
nor Baek Sung Min, just who...

102
00:07:09,626 --> 00:07:12,416
The initial response improvement plan,

103
00:07:12,417 --> 00:07:15,458
the one you sent after the briefing,

104
00:07:15,459 --> 00:07:17,416
it was impressive.

105
00:07:17,417 --> 00:07:19,791
It can help us improve our response practices.

106
00:07:19,792 --> 00:07:24,499
And also, it will help us win back public trust.

107
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:28,166
I only did what is required of me.

108
00:07:28,167 --> 00:07:32,375
What if we launch a pilot program
at Namgang Station?

109
00:07:36,709 --> 00:07:38,499
If it goes well,

110
00:07:38,500 --> 00:07:41,333
I will consider a full-scale adoption.

111
00:07:41,334 --> 00:07:43,374
Thank you, ma'am.

112
00:07:43,375 --> 00:07:45,000
Thank you.

113
00:07:49,667 --> 00:07:53,083
Let's go, Koo Gyeong Mo!

114
00:07:53,709 --> 00:07:58,208
Koo Gyeong Mo! Koo Gyeong Mo!

115
00:07:58,209 --> 00:08:00,209
It's you! It's all you!

116
00:08:00,834 --> 00:08:02,999
I'm sure your promotion is on it's way.

117
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:05,083
Thank you in advance.

118
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:16,959
Yes?

119
00:09:19,751 --> 00:09:22,333
The new Director is here to see you, ma'am.

120
00:09:22,334 --> 00:09:24,834
[Senior Superintendent Shin So Jung]
Oh, let her in.

121
00:09:31,834 --> 00:09:35,709
Detective Bureau Director Son Min A reporting.

122
00:09:37,250 --> 00:09:38,833
It's a pleasure, Director Son.

123
00:09:38,834 --> 00:09:42,041
Your reputation from the
Busan Narcotics Unit precedes you.

124
00:09:42,042 --> 00:09:44,499
I hope you bring that skill to your work here.

125
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:48,666
I will do my best to help the Division
check all the marks.

126
00:09:48,667 --> 00:09:50,625
What tea would you like?

127
00:09:50,626 --> 00:09:52,375
I'm good.

128
00:09:55,834 --> 00:09:56,917
Sis!

129
00:09:56,918 --> 00:10:00,208
Sis, sis, sis! It's been so long!

130
00:10:00,209 --> 00:10:01,291
You!

131
00:10:01,292 --> 00:10:03,625
You never called! Its been ages!

132
00:10:03,626 --> 00:10:05,541
You got a makeover?

133
00:10:05,542 --> 00:10:07,999
You're not so bad yourself.

134
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,750
There are so many narcotic cases.

135
00:10:10,751 --> 00:10:14,499
I was so busy chasing them around.

136
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:16,875
Oh, right. Hyun Kyung joined the force?

137
00:10:16,876 --> 00:10:18,499
- Don't even talk about it.
- Why?

138
00:10:18,500 --> 00:10:21,541
She's acting like a total stranger.
It's so frustrating.

139
00:10:21,542 --> 00:10:24,583
She thinks the world will end
if people find out I'm her mom.

140
00:10:24,584 --> 00:10:27,249
- You keep your mouth shut.
- All right, all right.

141
00:10:27,250 --> 00:10:29,958
She's trying to make it on her own.

142
00:10:29,959 --> 00:10:31,833
It's admirable.

143
00:10:31,834 --> 00:10:35,041
- Speaking of which, will you be okay?
- What?

144
00:10:35,042 --> 00:10:38,249
Now that you are here, you might bump into...

145
00:10:38,250 --> 00:10:40,458
You know...

146
00:10:40,459 --> 00:10:42,958
That was a long time ago.

147
00:10:42,959 --> 00:10:45,833
It's all in the past.

148
00:10:45,834 --> 00:10:48,249
- You sure?
- Dead sure.

149
00:10:48,250 --> 00:10:51,208
I am. It's written on my face.

150
00:10:51,209 --> 00:10:54,583
Anyway, I'm so happy you're here.

151
00:10:54,584 --> 00:10:55,625
Me, too!

152
00:10:55,626 --> 00:10:57,166
What's with the outfit?

153
00:10:57,167 --> 00:10:59,041
It's so not you. What happened?

154
00:10:59,042 --> 00:11:01,459
I wanted to look good for you.

155
00:11:02,417 --> 00:11:04,918
Yes, come in.

156
00:11:05,959 --> 00:11:08,209
Superintendent Lee is here to see you.

157
00:11:11,626 --> 00:11:13,333
Good to see you.

158
00:11:13,334 --> 00:11:15,333
You two haven't met, have you?

159
00:11:15,334 --> 00:11:18,792
This is Son Min A,
the new Detective Division Director.

160
00:11:24,876 --> 00:11:28,249
Son Min A. Superintendent Lee Tae Ju, right?

161
00:11:28,250 --> 00:11:31,875
Yes. Lee Tae Ju, from Violent Crimes.

162
00:11:31,876 --> 00:11:33,583
I heard a lot about you.

163
00:11:33,584 --> 00:11:34,875
What about?

164
00:11:34,876 --> 00:11:36,959
That I've got bad temper?

165
00:11:38,042 --> 00:11:40,249
That you always get the job done.

166
00:11:40,250 --> 00:11:42,625
No one remembers if there is no results.

167
00:11:42,626 --> 00:11:44,417
Victims, especially.

168
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:49,291
I asked around about you, too.

169
00:11:49,292 --> 00:11:53,375
You seem to be well connected,
with both politicians and businessmen.

170
00:11:56,209 --> 00:11:57,416
Yes.

171
00:11:57,417 --> 00:11:59,876
I like meeting people from all walks of like.

172
00:12:00,584 --> 00:12:03,583
I'm the opposite.

173
00:12:03,584 --> 00:12:08,124
When an officer likes meeting people too much,

174
00:12:08,125 --> 00:12:10,374
it invariably causes trouble.

175
00:12:10,375 --> 00:12:12,333
I'll keep that in mind.

176
00:12:12,334 --> 00:12:16,000
I'll be in my best behavior as a public servant.

177
00:12:19,667 --> 00:12:23,375
Okay, can you excuse us?

178
00:12:31,792 --> 00:12:33,541
He's that guy, right?

179
00:12:33,542 --> 00:12:35,918
Pyo Myeong Hak's right hand man.

180
00:12:37,042 --> 00:12:40,750
And the one who stabbed him in the back.

181
00:12:40,751 --> 00:12:42,708
Keep an eye on him.

182
00:12:42,709 --> 00:12:44,666
We just need to follow Lee Tae Ju,

183
00:12:44,667 --> 00:12:47,709
and he will lead us
to the lesion we must carve out.

184
00:12:49,792 --> 00:12:52,334
I'm so relieved you're here.

185
00:12:56,751 --> 00:12:59,583
I thought we could close the case
when we caught Cho Geun Won.

186
00:12:59,584 --> 00:13:01,249
Now we're back to square one.

187
00:13:01,250 --> 00:13:03,958
I haven't let him off the hook.

188
00:13:03,959 --> 00:13:07,499
I mean, one of the three suspects is dead,

189
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:09,791
another one almost died,

190
00:13:09,792 --> 00:13:11,166
Cho Geun Won is the only one left.

191
00:13:11,167 --> 00:13:13,082
His alibi checks out, though.

192
00:13:13,083 --> 00:13:14,333
You're right.

193
00:13:14,334 --> 00:13:16,708
I think it's strange, too.

194
00:13:16,709 --> 00:13:19,124
Except for us three,

195
00:13:19,125 --> 00:13:22,000
no one in our company has the required skills.

196
00:13:24,959 --> 00:13:26,334
And you are...

197
00:13:27,542 --> 00:13:29,000
not it, are you?

198
00:13:29,834 --> 00:13:33,666
Didn't you check my alibi?

199
00:13:33,667 --> 00:13:35,583
Yes, she was in the karaoke.

200
00:13:35,584 --> 00:13:37,541
You saw the CCTV footage.

201
00:13:37,542 --> 00:13:40,333
- You're right.
- What do you even sing?

202
00:13:40,334 --> 00:13:42,499
For three hours, alone?

203
00:13:42,500 --> 00:13:44,708
It's my hobby from college.

204
00:13:44,709 --> 00:13:47,375
Now, it's like a habit.

205
00:13:49,042 --> 00:13:52,250
It's my stress coping mechanism.

206
00:13:53,292 --> 00:13:54,875
Here's your kimchi jjigae.

207
00:13:54,876 --> 00:13:57,374
I could empty three bottles with this.

208
00:13:57,375 --> 00:13:59,708
Control yourself. The case is still open.

209
00:13:59,709 --> 00:14:03,291
Now that the food is here,
why don't we take a shot first?

210
00:14:03,292 --> 00:14:04,875
- Sure.
- Yeah.

211
00:14:04,876 --> 00:14:06,959
Cheers!

212
00:14:13,792 --> 00:14:17,167
Wow, Inspector Cha's friend,

213
00:14:17,959 --> 00:14:19,834
you sure can hold your liquor.

214
00:14:20,375 --> 00:14:23,584
Pace yourself. You live far from here.

215
00:14:25,209 --> 00:14:27,416
Don't worry.

216
00:14:27,417 --> 00:14:29,709
I can take care of myself.

217
00:14:36,292 --> 00:14:38,209
Eat, eat.

218
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,083
Okay.

219
00:14:56,209 --> 00:14:58,834
[Traffic Civil Petition 24]

220
00:15:02,125 --> 00:15:04,500
[Accident: Search results]

221
00:15:08,167 --> 00:15:10,834
[Auto-bicycle collision]

222
00:15:19,292 --> 00:15:23,082
I knew she was drinking too fast.

223
00:15:23,083 --> 00:15:25,625
Ji Yoon, you okay? Need help?

224
00:15:25,626 --> 00:15:27,416
I'm fine!

225
00:15:27,417 --> 00:15:29,334
I'm almost done.

226
00:15:30,375 --> 00:15:32,917
She is far from done.

227
00:15:32,918 --> 00:15:34,584
Gosh.

228
00:15:39,667 --> 00:15:41,082
Feeling better?

229
00:15:41,083 --> 00:15:43,500
Yes, I emptied it all out.

230
00:15:45,250 --> 00:15:46,999
I'm really sorry.

231
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:48,958
To you, and your father, too.

232
00:15:48,959 --> 00:15:51,374
Well, you should be.

233
00:15:51,375 --> 00:15:54,124
Buy me a drink sometime, if you're sorry.

234
00:15:54,125 --> 00:15:56,834
Sure. I'll buy you a drink...

235
00:15:58,834 --> 00:16:00,833
No, let's just eat. Food.

236
00:16:00,834 --> 00:16:02,249
Just food.

237
00:16:02,250 --> 00:16:03,834
Whatever you like.

238
00:16:05,709 --> 00:16:08,249
Now, go to bed.

239
00:16:08,250 --> 00:16:10,583
You can sleep here.

240
00:16:10,584 --> 00:16:12,958
Such a long day. So long.

241
00:16:12,959 --> 00:16:14,208
I'll turn the light off.

242
00:16:14,209 --> 00:16:15,500
Okay.

243
00:16:16,083 --> 00:16:18,876
And, thank you.

244
00:16:19,834 --> 00:16:21,499
What for?

245
00:16:21,500 --> 00:16:24,958
I was too overwhelmed to thank you properly,

246
00:16:24,959 --> 00:16:26,959
for saving me, I mean.

247
00:16:28,709 --> 00:16:30,291
You are amazing.

248
00:16:30,292 --> 00:16:32,124
You could have been hurt.

249
00:16:32,125 --> 00:16:34,334
But you threw yourself into danger.

250
00:16:36,042 --> 00:16:38,667
Because I don't want to regret it.

251
00:16:39,626 --> 00:16:41,791
I don't want anyone

252
00:16:41,792 --> 00:16:44,918
to get hurt or die on my account.

253
00:16:51,918 --> 00:16:55,292
[How to build self-driving cars]

254
00:17:03,542 --> 00:17:05,751
Who is this?

255
00:17:08,667 --> 00:17:11,542
My first mentor, from when I joined the force.

256
00:17:12,459 --> 00:17:14,041
You look like sisters.

257
00:17:14,042 --> 00:17:16,042
Where is she now?

258
00:17:17,626 --> 00:17:20,000
She died, because of me.

259
00:17:24,959 --> 00:17:28,000
Who calls at this hour?

260
00:17:31,167 --> 00:17:32,834
Yes, Investigator Cha.

261
00:17:34,417 --> 00:17:35,834
Huh?

262
00:17:40,542 --> 00:17:44,458
Do you have to do this now?

263
00:17:44,459 --> 00:17:47,334
Ji Yoon was up all night throwing-

264
00:17:50,959 --> 00:17:54,208
It's the only way to prove my theory.

265
00:17:54,209 --> 00:17:56,249
And it's safer

266
00:17:56,250 --> 00:17:58,375
when there is no car around.

267
00:17:59,083 --> 00:18:01,124
- Ready?
- Yeah.

268
00:18:01,125 --> 00:18:04,625
Wait, wait. It's gonna stop, right?

269
00:18:04,626 --> 00:18:05,833
Right?

270
00:18:05,834 --> 00:18:08,958
Well, I haven't done this before.

271
00:18:08,959 --> 00:18:11,041
I'll start the car.

272
00:18:11,042 --> 00:18:12,334
Okay.

273
00:18:29,375 --> 00:18:32,083
- Stop the car!
- The brake is not working!

274
00:18:41,500 --> 00:18:43,249
We stopped.

275
00:18:43,250 --> 00:18:44,750
Thank god we're alive.

276
00:18:44,751 --> 00:18:46,875
Are you all right? Good job.

277
00:18:46,876 --> 00:18:49,374
Good work.

278
00:18:49,375 --> 00:18:51,917
Shall we do it again, just in case?

279
00:18:51,918 --> 00:18:53,417
Huh?

280
00:18:58,417 --> 00:19:00,291
Lee Do Hyun was the target?

281
00:19:00,292 --> 00:19:02,291
I'm saying he could have been.

282
00:19:02,292 --> 00:19:05,499
Who would target Lee Do Hyun? And why?

283
00:19:05,500 --> 00:19:09,917
I checked the accident records,
and found another one in February.

284
00:19:09,918 --> 00:19:12,249
Han Soo In's car hit Lee Do Hyun,

285
00:19:12,250 --> 00:19:13,625
while he was riding a bicycle.

286
00:19:13,626 --> 00:19:16,917
Lee Do Hyun, of all people?
Talk about bad coincidence.

287
00:19:16,918 --> 00:19:18,625
Two accidents in a row?

288
00:19:18,626 --> 00:19:21,041
I asked the insurer, and

289
00:19:21,042 --> 00:19:24,416
these two argued over fault allocation.

290
00:19:24,417 --> 00:19:27,917
More like, Lee Do Hyun was giving her
a hard time over the fault issue.

291
00:19:27,918 --> 00:19:31,791
Are you saying Han Soo In could have
killed Lee Do Hyun because of that?

292
00:19:31,792 --> 00:19:33,166
Even if she had the motive,

293
00:19:33,167 --> 00:19:35,958
she didn't have the skills.

294
00:19:35,959 --> 00:19:38,082
Yeah, she would have had to

295
00:19:38,083 --> 00:19:40,291
- tinker with the self-driving algorithm.
- You're right.

296
00:19:40,292 --> 00:19:42,583
- What?
- Right about what?

297
00:19:42,584 --> 00:19:45,541
Right about Han Soo In lacking the skills,
or about Baek Sung Min helping her?

298
00:19:45,542 --> 00:19:46,875
Without Baek Sung Min's help,

299
00:19:46,876 --> 00:19:48,833
it would not have been possible.

300
00:19:48,834 --> 00:19:53,458
With both Cho Geun Won and Yoon Ji Yoon
removed from the suspect list,

301
00:19:53,459 --> 00:19:56,374
The only one capable of committing
this crime is Baek Sung Min.

302
00:19:56,375 --> 00:20:00,417
But Baek Sung Min is dead.
He was killed in the accident.

303
00:20:01,209 --> 00:20:03,833
What is for sure, is that for this crime to work,

304
00:20:03,834 --> 00:20:06,583
Baek Sung Min must be involved.

305
00:20:06,584 --> 00:20:07,958
To put it simply,

306
00:20:07,959 --> 00:20:12,208
he's like a 'necessary condition'
that makes the proposition true.

307
00:20:12,209 --> 00:20:13,875
How's that 'simple'?

308
00:20:13,876 --> 00:20:17,499
Whatever it is, Baek Sung Min was involved?

309
00:20:17,500 --> 00:20:18,708
Yes.

310
00:20:18,709 --> 00:20:21,666
However, killing a man over fault allocation,

311
00:20:21,667 --> 00:20:24,708
is not a valid motive for murder.

312
00:20:24,709 --> 00:20:27,708
I think we need to look into the relationship

313
00:20:27,709 --> 00:20:30,417
between Han Soo In, Baek Sung Min
and Lee Do Hyun.

314
00:20:32,918 --> 00:20:35,334
[Driver: Han Soo In]

315
00:20:38,125 --> 00:20:39,583
I heard about the case.

316
00:20:39,584 --> 00:20:42,416
So, someone hacked the car?

317
00:20:42,417 --> 00:20:44,958
Yes. This is the black box from the car.

318
00:20:44,959 --> 00:20:47,958
Can you restore the deleted data?

319
00:20:47,959 --> 00:20:51,041
Didn't you have them restored already?

320
00:20:51,042 --> 00:20:54,458
We focused on driver error at the time,

321
00:20:54,459 --> 00:20:56,374
so we didn't do a full restoration.

322
00:20:56,375 --> 00:20:59,499
Okay. I will do my best.

323
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:01,166
Thank you.

324
00:21:01,167 --> 00:21:03,583
How's the Captain doing?

325
00:21:03,584 --> 00:21:05,542
Just his normal self.

326
00:21:07,209 --> 00:21:11,917
Oh, I was going to contact him.

327
00:21:11,918 --> 00:21:14,208
It's about his wife's case.

328
00:21:14,209 --> 00:21:17,375
I think DNA amplification might help.

329
00:21:19,083 --> 00:21:20,833
What are you talking about?

330
00:21:20,834 --> 00:21:23,083
Oh, you didn't know.

331
00:21:23,751 --> 00:21:27,750
Captain Jung is still on the hit-and-run case.

332
00:21:27,751 --> 00:21:30,499
He comes here every time
a similar accident occurred,

333
00:21:30,500 --> 00:21:32,626
asking about DNA evidence.

334
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:36,041
At his wife's scene of accident,

335
00:21:36,042 --> 00:21:40,499
we found some DNA that may belong to the driver.

336
00:21:40,500 --> 00:21:43,791
We couldn't analyze it at the time.

337
00:21:43,792 --> 00:21:47,375
Now, we have the tech to amplify it.

338
00:21:54,751 --> 00:21:57,167
[Call Detail Records]

339
00:22:34,709 --> 00:22:37,124
Why is there no egg?

340
00:22:37,125 --> 00:22:38,416
You already ate it.

341
00:22:38,417 --> 00:22:40,000
I did?

342
00:22:53,375 --> 00:22:54,791
Lieutenant.

343
00:22:54,792 --> 00:22:56,876
Have some drinks.

344
00:22:58,834 --> 00:23:01,042
Thank you.

345
00:23:05,334 --> 00:23:07,166
Nice drink.

346
00:23:07,167 --> 00:23:09,000
Man, it's good.

347
00:23:11,375 --> 00:23:12,958
Take a seat.

348
00:23:12,959 --> 00:23:15,042
Oh, okay.

349
00:23:17,709 --> 00:23:19,041
How's work treating you?

350
00:23:19,042 --> 00:23:22,583
I think I found the right job.

351
00:23:22,584 --> 00:23:24,125
Glad to hear it.

352
00:23:27,667 --> 00:23:30,666
I heard you nagged Superintendent Yeom so hard

353
00:23:30,667 --> 00:23:32,833
to assign you to our team.

354
00:23:32,834 --> 00:23:34,750
Yes, I did.

355
00:23:34,751 --> 00:23:36,333
Why do you want to work with us?

356
00:23:36,334 --> 00:23:39,791
I think what you do here is so cool,

357
00:23:39,792 --> 00:23:41,875
and it looks kind of fun, actually.

358
00:23:41,876 --> 00:23:44,375
Also, I have so many questions.

359
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:46,791
What about?

360
00:23:46,792 --> 00:23:49,876
About many things.

361
00:23:55,959 --> 00:23:58,833
Well, I don't know.

362
00:23:58,834 --> 00:24:01,166
It may look like it, but

363
00:24:01,167 --> 00:24:04,166
it's not all fun and games here.

364
00:24:04,167 --> 00:24:08,541
Sometimes, it's so hard I can't take it.

365
00:24:08,542 --> 00:24:10,499
Sometimes,

366
00:24:10,500 --> 00:24:13,499
I just want to run away.

367
00:24:13,500 --> 00:24:15,166
Sometimes,

368
00:24:15,167 --> 00:24:18,792
it feels it's worth all that.

369
00:24:21,125 --> 00:24:23,833
Well, just hang tight.

370
00:24:23,834 --> 00:24:26,708
Who knows? You may work here after training.

371
00:24:26,709 --> 00:24:28,499
I'll do my best.

372
00:24:28,500 --> 00:24:30,667
Thanks for the drink.

373
00:24:55,751 --> 00:24:58,625
Look at this. This is Han Soo In's black box data.

374
00:24:58,626 --> 00:25:02,208
Han Soo In visited the same place three times
in the past month.

375
00:25:02,209 --> 00:25:03,750
Including the day before the crash.

376
00:25:03,751 --> 00:25:05,416
Where is that?

377
00:25:05,417 --> 00:25:07,291
It's near Paldang Dam.

378
00:25:07,292 --> 00:25:10,166
Why go there? There's nothing there.

379
00:25:10,167 --> 00:25:11,583
Hold on a minute.

380
00:25:11,584 --> 00:25:13,625
Is it Joan-myeon, Namyangju-si?

381
00:25:13,626 --> 00:25:15,625
I checked the taxi payment records,

382
00:25:15,626 --> 00:25:17,583
Baek Sung Min was there before the crash.

383
00:25:17,584 --> 00:25:20,167
- Time?
- Around 3 p.m.

384
00:25:20,876 --> 00:25:22,333
[Joan-myeon, Namyangju-si]

385
00:25:22,334 --> 00:25:24,625
Baek Sung Min and Han Soo In
visited the dam before the crash,

386
00:25:24,626 --> 00:25:27,499
but they went there separately.

387
00:25:27,500 --> 00:25:30,875
To meet up there and plan the murder?

388
00:25:30,876 --> 00:25:34,584
Why would they do it there?
They could discuss it at home.

389
00:25:35,500 --> 00:25:38,041
Maybe it was a plan that required some practice.

390
00:25:38,042 --> 00:25:40,751
Like, killing someone with a car.

391
00:25:41,667 --> 00:25:42,876
[Joan-myeon, Namyangju-si]

392
00:26:09,459 --> 00:26:13,459
Why did Han Soo In come here?
Not just once, but three times?

393
00:26:15,584 --> 00:26:17,750
CCTV.

394
00:26:17,751 --> 00:26:20,250
Let's split up and look for it.

395
00:26:21,250 --> 00:26:22,959
Let's go, let's go.

396
00:26:32,334 --> 00:26:33,499
Detective Eo?

397
00:26:33,500 --> 00:26:34,750
What is it?

398
00:26:34,751 --> 00:26:37,041
Do you have some time?

399
00:26:37,042 --> 00:26:38,499
Time?

400
00:26:38,500 --> 00:26:41,249
I found something that stands out.

401
00:26:41,250 --> 00:26:43,834
Can you come with me for a minute?

402
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:14,958
I found a CCTV camera.

403
00:27:14,959 --> 00:27:16,500
Wait, wait.

404
00:27:17,417 --> 00:27:19,625
You better wait here. Let me go alone.

405
00:27:19,626 --> 00:27:21,833
Why? I'll go with you.

406
00:27:21,834 --> 00:27:24,500
It's a urology clinic. And you are...

407
00:27:25,083 --> 00:27:26,416
A woman?

408
00:27:26,417 --> 00:27:28,499
Women have urinal systems, too.

409
00:27:28,500 --> 00:27:29,708
Move!

410
00:27:29,709 --> 00:27:32,082
Please. I'll be real quick.

411
00:27:32,083 --> 00:27:33,833
You can't block the entrance.

412
00:27:33,834 --> 00:27:35,333
We are police. Here for an investigation.

413
00:27:35,334 --> 00:27:37,333
Not that I have any issues.

414
00:27:37,334 --> 00:27:39,208
Okay, come in.

415
00:27:39,209 --> 00:27:40,918
Won't take long.

416
00:27:46,751 --> 00:27:50,583
1st April, 3:12 p.m, here.

417
00:27:50,584 --> 00:27:53,083
- Play it faster.
- Okay.

418
00:27:56,459 --> 00:27:58,291
What is she doing? DUI?

419
00:27:58,292 --> 00:28:00,292
Let's watch a bit longer.

420
00:28:07,542 --> 00:28:09,333
She had company.

421
00:28:09,334 --> 00:28:11,249
Looks like a man. Is it the husband?

422
00:28:11,250 --> 00:28:12,958
It can't be him.

423
00:28:12,959 --> 00:28:14,625
He went there by taxi.

424
00:28:14,626 --> 00:28:16,416
Who, then?

425
00:28:16,417 --> 00:28:18,999
Do we have Lee Do Hyun's
cell site access records?

426
00:28:19,000 --> 00:28:21,375
Yes, I do.

427
00:28:25,876 --> 00:28:27,250
Here.

428
00:28:31,375 --> 00:28:34,751
The cell site is in Joan-myeon.

429
00:28:36,083 --> 00:28:37,458
Then it means that man is...

430
00:28:37,459 --> 00:28:40,041
If Lee Do Hyun and Han Soo In were together,

431
00:28:40,042 --> 00:28:43,000
their relationship might be something
we didn't expect.

432
00:28:44,292 --> 00:28:45,875
- Jackpot!
- You scared me!

433
00:28:45,876 --> 00:28:47,416
We hit the jackpot.

434
00:28:47,417 --> 00:28:48,750
What are you fussing about?

435
00:28:48,751 --> 00:28:52,333
The baby Han Soo In is carrying,
is not Baek Sung Min's.

436
00:28:52,334 --> 00:28:54,708
Baek Sung Min is not the father?
What are you talking about?

437
00:28:54,709 --> 00:28:57,416
Baek Sung Min's credit card records
showed visits to an urology clinic.

438
00:28:57,417 --> 00:28:58,499
So we went to check.

439
00:28:58,500 --> 00:29:00,208
Baek Sung Min can't have babies.

440
00:29:00,209 --> 00:29:02,459
That's right. He's...

441
00:29:03,751 --> 00:29:05,666
- Infertile!
- Infertile?

442
00:29:05,667 --> 00:29:06,875
[Diagnosed with azoospermia]

443
00:29:06,876 --> 00:29:08,499
This is crazy.

444
00:29:08,500 --> 00:29:10,666
Now I get the picture.

445
00:29:10,667 --> 00:29:12,708
The first accident was not just bad luck.

446
00:29:12,709 --> 00:29:15,000
They were already seeing each other.

447
00:29:16,959 --> 00:29:18,666
Get a statement from her.

448
00:29:18,667 --> 00:29:21,124
I'll go. Inspector Cha, you're with me.

449
00:29:21,125 --> 00:29:22,584
Nice one.

450
00:29:25,792 --> 00:29:28,791
Dae Se!

451
00:29:28,792 --> 00:29:31,917
You did great.

452
00:29:31,918 --> 00:29:34,584
Good for you.

453
00:29:36,125 --> 00:29:38,334
I'm glad to see you're well.

454
00:29:39,167 --> 00:29:41,959
It was not a serious injury.

455
00:29:43,709 --> 00:29:46,334
About Lee Do Hyun, the one who passed,

456
00:29:47,334 --> 00:29:50,416
Records say you had met him
a year before the accident,

457
00:29:50,417 --> 00:29:53,667
because of a fender-bender
between your car and his bicycle.

458
00:29:55,250 --> 00:29:58,500
Yes, but I didn't know his name at the time.

459
00:29:59,626 --> 00:30:02,124
Did you see him after the first accident?

460
00:30:02,125 --> 00:30:04,584
There's no reason for me to.

461
00:30:05,125 --> 00:30:07,000
No, I didn't.

462
00:30:18,125 --> 00:30:20,791
This is Dr. Baek's physical exam records.

463
00:30:20,792 --> 00:30:23,999
Dr. Baek could not have babies.

464
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:26,124
He was infertile.

465
00:30:26,125 --> 00:30:30,334
We know you are pregnant,
so we went to the hospital to check.

466
00:30:32,167 --> 00:30:34,291
The child.

467
00:30:34,292 --> 00:30:36,292
Lee Do Hyun's the father, isn't he?

468
00:30:37,834 --> 00:30:40,958
Dr. Baek knew what was going on
between you two.

469
00:30:40,959 --> 00:30:44,666
He followed you to Paldang Dam,
where you used to meet in secret.

470
00:30:44,667 --> 00:30:47,625
He must have watched you for a long time.

471
00:30:47,626 --> 00:30:50,666
That was the motive for this crime.

472
00:30:50,667 --> 00:30:52,751
I can't believe it.

473
00:30:53,417 --> 00:30:56,166
I can't believe he did such a terrible thing.

474
00:30:56,167 --> 00:30:58,751
Which is more terrible?

475
00:30:59,334 --> 00:31:03,291
Trying to keep him in the dark
when you carry another's baby?

476
00:31:03,292 --> 00:31:04,625
Or,

477
00:31:04,626 --> 00:31:08,918
planning a murder
out of vengeance and humiliation?

478
00:31:18,417 --> 00:31:21,918
[Deceased: Lee Do Hyun]

479
00:31:27,500 --> 00:31:29,792
They died because of me.

480
00:31:32,584 --> 00:31:34,959
I had to stop.

481
00:31:38,500 --> 00:31:40,876
It's all because of me.

482
00:32:07,918 --> 00:32:09,666
Investigator Cha, do you have some coins?

483
00:32:09,667 --> 00:32:11,209
No.

484
00:32:22,667 --> 00:32:25,000
I can't believe it.

485
00:32:25,709 --> 00:32:29,000
Dr. Baek seemed like a good researcher.

486
00:32:29,918 --> 00:32:32,999
How could he plan something so cruel?

487
00:32:33,000 --> 00:32:35,750
I think he was living in a hell

488
00:32:35,751 --> 00:32:38,751
that he created in his mind.

489
00:32:40,375 --> 00:32:43,750
He did something that he felt

490
00:32:43,751 --> 00:32:45,917
was the only way out of there.

491
00:32:45,918 --> 00:32:48,875
So she lied through her teeth
the whole time.

492
00:32:48,876 --> 00:32:53,041
Cheating is bad enough,
but this is beyond my grasp.

493
00:32:53,042 --> 00:32:55,000
Who did what?

494
00:32:55,626 --> 00:32:58,458
Who cheats on his wife when she's pregnant?

495
00:32:58,459 --> 00:33:02,416
- No one said that. Literally no one.
- Gotta break all his bones.

496
00:33:02,417 --> 00:33:04,458
Starting with his legs.

497
00:33:04,459 --> 00:33:06,750
And then work up his body.

498
00:33:06,751 --> 00:33:09,333
Break'em like twigs.

499
00:33:09,334 --> 00:33:12,082
Don't listen to your mother, little one.

500
00:33:12,083 --> 00:33:14,999
Good thoughts, nice thoughts.

501
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:16,999
There, there.

502
00:33:17,000 --> 00:33:19,166
Thank God you're here.

503
00:33:19,167 --> 00:33:21,249
Do you have a coin?

504
00:33:21,250 --> 00:33:24,499
How dare you.

505
00:33:24,500 --> 00:33:27,458
You're extorting a pregnant woman.

506
00:33:27,459 --> 00:33:29,666
- Pretty please?
- Here.

507
00:33:29,667 --> 00:33:31,500
Thank you, ma'am.

508
00:33:33,417 --> 00:33:34,917
What a waste.

509
00:33:34,918 --> 00:33:38,042
It's okay. I've got more.

510
00:33:49,250 --> 00:33:50,876
Could it be?

511
00:33:53,500 --> 00:33:56,417
I have to be somewhere.

512
00:34:02,334 --> 00:34:04,541
Wait! Stop that for a second.

513
00:34:04,542 --> 00:34:05,750
- Is that the one?
- Yeah.

514
00:34:05,751 --> 00:34:07,958
We're from the police.

515
00:34:07,959 --> 00:34:09,541
So sorry, sir.

516
00:34:09,542 --> 00:34:11,584
Just hurry, okay?

517
00:34:13,083 --> 00:34:15,375
- Is it there?
- Hold on a minute.

518
00:34:28,083 --> 00:34:31,000
I have nothing else to say.

519
00:34:31,542 --> 00:34:33,209
Ms. Han,

520
00:34:33,876 --> 00:34:35,791
at Paldang Dam,

521
00:34:35,792 --> 00:34:40,499
there is a ramp that goes into the river.
Why did you go there?

522
00:34:40,500 --> 00:34:42,041
Well.

523
00:34:42,042 --> 00:34:43,750
We went for a drive.

524
00:34:43,751 --> 00:34:45,416
Went for a drive?

525
00:34:45,417 --> 00:34:47,417
Was that all?

526
00:34:48,375 --> 00:34:50,374
That's right.

527
00:34:50,375 --> 00:34:52,584
Could there be anything else?

528
00:35:05,292 --> 00:35:06,666
Now, don't forget.

529
00:35:06,667 --> 00:35:09,374
Put the wheel on the center line,

530
00:35:09,375 --> 00:35:11,791
and shift into neutral.

531
00:35:11,792 --> 00:35:15,999
Then turn the steering left and right,
and the car will slide off.

532
00:35:16,000 --> 00:35:18,291
Now, this is important.

533
00:35:18,292 --> 00:35:20,625
Leave the driver side window open,

534
00:35:20,626 --> 00:35:23,041
and lock the passenger side window.

535
00:35:23,042 --> 00:35:26,166
And you must stay in the water
as long as possible

536
00:35:26,167 --> 00:35:28,541
before you escape to the surface.

537
00:35:28,542 --> 00:35:30,042
Okay?

538
00:35:34,042 --> 00:35:36,167
But...

539
00:35:38,709 --> 00:35:40,542
wouldn't he wake up?

540
00:35:41,792 --> 00:35:43,374
Babe,

541
00:35:43,375 --> 00:35:46,917
we're talking about wine with two sleeping pills.

542
00:35:46,918 --> 00:35:49,374
An elephant wouldn't wake up.

543
00:35:49,375 --> 00:35:52,751
And you said he takes the pills all the time.

544
00:35:55,417 --> 00:35:57,583
What do I say to the police?

545
00:35:57,584 --> 00:36:00,666
They will think it's an accident.

546
00:36:00,667 --> 00:36:02,166
Let's go over it again.

547
00:36:02,167 --> 00:36:05,999
You went for a drive with him,
and the car slipped.

548
00:36:06,000 --> 00:36:09,082
I barely made it out,

549
00:36:09,083 --> 00:36:11,499
but my poor husband did not.

550
00:36:11,500 --> 00:36:13,791
Won't they be suspicious?

551
00:36:13,792 --> 00:36:16,124
What is there to suspect?

552
00:36:16,125 --> 00:36:20,167
Even if they are suspicious,
your father has your back.

553
00:36:21,667 --> 00:36:25,625
I think your father would be glad

554
00:36:25,626 --> 00:36:27,667
to get him out of the picture.

555
00:36:30,876 --> 00:36:34,833
Are you sure about the insurance claim?

556
00:36:34,834 --> 00:36:36,374
Come on.

557
00:36:36,375 --> 00:36:38,958
It's 100% failproof. It's not a suicide.

558
00:36:38,959 --> 00:36:40,375
Also...

559
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:47,751
Your pregnancy will help us
persuade the insurance guys.

560
00:36:49,709 --> 00:36:51,875
I'm so scared.

561
00:36:51,876 --> 00:36:54,959
Are you sure this is the only way?

562
00:36:56,125 --> 00:36:57,958
Babe,

563
00:36:57,959 --> 00:36:59,333
this is for us,

564
00:36:59,334 --> 00:37:03,833
and the baby in there.

565
00:37:03,834 --> 00:37:06,250
Baek Sung Min must die.

566
00:37:41,667 --> 00:37:45,791
I found this listening device
in your car, Ms. Han.

567
00:37:45,792 --> 00:37:49,249
Dr. Baek had been listening
to what you were saying in the car

568
00:37:49,250 --> 00:37:51,875
through his mobile phone.

569
00:37:51,876 --> 00:37:53,374
He heard everything,

570
00:37:53,375 --> 00:37:55,792
including the plan to murder him.

571
00:38:00,542 --> 00:38:03,208
I didn't plan to kill him.

572
00:38:03,209 --> 00:38:07,583
Do Hyun kept talking about it,
so I just played along.

573
00:38:07,584 --> 00:38:10,458
I wasn't going to really do it.

574
00:38:10,459 --> 00:38:13,709
- It was like a joke-
- Look, Han Soo In.

575
00:38:14,959 --> 00:38:17,833
You didn't just cheat on your husband,
you even planned to kill him.

576
00:38:17,834 --> 00:38:20,792
It was all recorded, and this is
still what you are saying?

577
00:38:39,334 --> 00:38:41,208
Dr. Baek, who found out that

578
00:38:41,209 --> 00:38:45,417
his wife was trying to kill him.

579
00:38:46,042 --> 00:38:48,626
Try to think what he must have felt.

580
00:39:00,167 --> 00:39:03,000
Dr. Baek planned his revenge.

581
00:39:04,250 --> 00:39:06,917
He devised a plan for his wife
who planned to kill him.

582
00:39:06,918 --> 00:39:09,499
A plan to have her kill her own lover,

583
00:39:09,500 --> 00:39:12,541
and even himself.

584
00:39:12,542 --> 00:39:15,292
A fatally elaborate plan.

585
00:39:37,667 --> 00:39:39,625
Okay.

586
00:39:39,626 --> 00:39:41,833
I cheated on him.

587
00:39:41,834 --> 00:39:45,833
I admit it. But that isn't a crime.

588
00:39:45,834 --> 00:39:49,583
Bottom line is, my husband killed Do Hyun,

589
00:39:49,584 --> 00:39:52,417
and took his own life.

590
00:39:55,125 --> 00:39:58,041
I think we're done talking.

591
00:39:58,042 --> 00:39:59,917
I'm leaving.

592
00:39:59,918 --> 00:40:01,876
Sit down.

593
00:40:02,834 --> 00:40:05,958
Plotting to kill is a crime in itself.

594
00:40:05,959 --> 00:40:08,751
It's called premeditation, you know?

595
00:40:20,250 --> 00:40:24,000
We found this in Dr. Baek's office desk.

596
00:40:34,459 --> 00:40:36,291
<i>Dear baby.</i>

597
00:40:36,292 --> 00:40:40,917
<i>I wonder what you are thinking
in your mom's belly.</i>

598
00:40:40,918 --> 00:40:46,666
<i>I'm planting seeds of love in your heart.</i>

599
00:40:46,667 --> 00:40:48,499
<i>With love, your Dad.</i>

600
00:40:48,500 --> 00:40:52,708
Forensically speaking,
Dr. Baek took his own life.

601
00:40:52,709 --> 00:40:56,875
But I think there's more to it.

602
00:40:56,876 --> 00:40:59,666
He was killed.

603
00:40:59,667 --> 00:41:02,166
By his wife,

604
00:41:02,167 --> 00:41:03,708
and the ones closest to him,

605
00:41:03,709 --> 00:41:05,958
quietly,

606
00:41:05,959 --> 00:41:08,000
ever so slowly.

607
00:41:15,209 --> 00:41:17,999
I will call my father.

608
00:41:18,000 --> 00:41:19,583
You're in trouble.

609
00:41:19,584 --> 00:41:22,166
I'm not saying another word without my lawyer.

610
00:41:22,167 --> 00:41:24,208
Yeah, suit yourself.

611
00:41:24,209 --> 00:41:26,917
Make that call.

612
00:41:26,918 --> 00:41:30,166
But put these on, first. Don't move. It'll hurt.

613
00:41:30,167 --> 00:41:31,834
I mean it.

614
00:41:32,876 --> 00:41:34,541
Now, call your dad.

615
00:41:34,542 --> 00:41:36,709
Okay? Do it.

616
00:42:20,792 --> 00:42:22,291
[Seoul Namgang Police Station]

617
00:42:22,292 --> 00:42:24,583
[Investigation]

618
00:42:24,584 --> 00:42:25,959
[Sign In]

619
00:42:35,500 --> 00:42:37,666
[ID: Dong Gi]

620
00:42:37,667 --> 00:42:41,959
[General search]

621
00:42:43,751 --> 00:42:45,333
[Officer shot]

622
00:42:45,334 --> 00:42:48,041
[3 April 2016, Daejeon Hwado Station]

623
00:42:48,042 --> 00:42:51,417
[Firearm stolen and officer shot to death]

624
00:42:55,667 --> 00:42:57,750
<i>During patrol, Lieutenant Park Hae Ok</i>

625
00:42:57,751 --> 00:43:00,374
<i>was attacked while approaching a suspect vehicle.</i>

626
00:43:00,375 --> 00:43:02,208
<i>Lieutenant Park was...</i>

627
00:43:02,209 --> 00:43:03,249
Stop!

628
00:43:03,250 --> 00:43:06,499
<i>Run over by the vehicle
and shot to death by the suspect.</i>

629
00:43:06,500 --> 00:43:08,751
<i>Her partner failed to aid her.</i>

630
00:43:10,542 --> 00:43:13,833
<i>Partner Min So Hee was also
attacked while responding on the scene.</i>

631
00:43:13,834 --> 00:43:15,333
Drop the gun!

632
00:43:15,334 --> 00:43:18,708
<i>Min So Hee was carrying a gun,</i>

633
00:43:18,709 --> 00:43:23,000
<i>but failed to respond in time.</i>

634
00:43:32,375 --> 00:43:34,626
[Seoul Namgang Police Station]

635
00:43:35,751 --> 00:43:37,459
Okay.

636
00:43:52,042 --> 00:43:54,083
[Faster response, unwavering strength]

637
00:43:55,125 --> 00:43:59,999
Man, I thought you worked out!

638
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:03,625
You won't even pass the qualification!

639
00:44:03,626 --> 00:44:05,666
I didn't sleep well.

640
00:44:05,667 --> 00:44:08,458
Why? Something's on your mind?

641
00:44:08,459 --> 00:44:10,750
Just some thoughts.

642
00:44:10,751 --> 00:44:12,416
Gosh.

643
00:44:12,417 --> 00:44:14,249
I will help you

644
00:44:14,250 --> 00:44:16,209
sleep like a baby today.

645
00:44:17,167 --> 00:44:18,834
Investigator Cha!

646
00:44:19,667 --> 00:44:21,541
No, you're not done.

647
00:44:21,542 --> 00:44:22,750
- Hey!
- Too early.

648
00:44:22,751 --> 00:44:25,249
Can't breathe!

649
00:44:25,250 --> 00:44:27,167
Just tap!

650
00:44:28,125 --> 00:44:30,167
You trying to kill him?

651
00:44:32,792 --> 00:44:34,249
Hey!

652
00:44:34,250 --> 00:44:35,791
You should have tapped.

653
00:44:35,792 --> 00:44:37,833
- I can't.
- Why not? Use this hand!

654
00:44:37,834 --> 00:44:39,374
I can't.

655
00:44:39,375 --> 00:44:41,125
You try it.

656
00:44:44,584 --> 00:44:46,666
Are you really letting him teach Dae Se?

657
00:44:46,667 --> 00:44:47,958
Why not do it yourself?

658
00:44:47,959 --> 00:44:49,958
What's wrong with letting Inspector Cha do it?

659
00:44:49,959 --> 00:44:53,791
I just can't imagine him teaching anyone.

660
00:44:53,792 --> 00:44:56,124
Right? I mean, it's a martial art.

661
00:44:56,125 --> 00:44:58,791
He's got no muscle, either.

662
00:44:58,792 --> 00:45:01,166
He is not what he used to be.

663
00:45:01,167 --> 00:45:03,374
He's been working out.

664
00:45:03,375 --> 00:45:08,876
Plus, he likes teaching others.

665
00:45:14,792 --> 00:45:16,291
Now,

666
00:45:16,292 --> 00:45:19,625
MMA fighter Wanderlei Simba said...

667
00:45:19,626 --> 00:45:22,666
MMA fighter Wanderlei Silva said,

668
00:45:22,667 --> 00:45:25,041
I don't fight with techniques.
I fight with my heart.

669
00:45:25,042 --> 00:45:27,917
He said, I don't fight with techniques.

670
00:45:27,918 --> 00:45:29,666
I fight with my heart.

671
00:45:29,667 --> 00:45:32,708
Fighting is all about the spirit.

672
00:45:32,709 --> 00:45:34,958
It's Silva.

673
00:45:34,959 --> 00:45:37,374
Silva. Not Simba.

674
00:45:37,375 --> 00:45:40,791
Simba is the lion from Lion King.

675
00:45:40,792 --> 00:45:43,709
Ah, Silva. Of course.

676
00:45:44,626 --> 00:45:49,166
Police arrest tactics are designed
to arrest and suppress criminals.

677
00:45:49,167 --> 00:45:52,333
However, what's more important

678
00:45:52,334 --> 00:45:54,917
is to protect yourself from resistance.

679
00:45:54,918 --> 00:45:56,750
If you get hurt,

680
00:45:56,751 --> 00:45:59,834
you lose the chance to put handcuffs.

681
00:46:03,209 --> 00:46:04,291
All right.

682
00:46:04,292 --> 00:46:05,625
Train as if it's a real fight.

683
00:46:05,626 --> 00:46:08,042
If you make me fall, training's over.

684
00:46:16,209 --> 00:46:17,999
Good.

685
00:46:18,000 --> 00:46:19,751
Bring it on.

686
00:47:01,876 --> 00:47:03,791
That's how he got me!

687
00:47:17,209 --> 00:47:18,876
Terrible, isn't it?

688
00:47:19,918 --> 00:47:22,166
Hurt, utterly helpless.

689
00:47:22,167 --> 00:47:24,416
Belittled,

690
00:47:24,417 --> 00:47:26,041
utterly helpless.

691
00:47:26,042 --> 00:47:28,166
The feeling like you're worthless?

692
00:47:28,167 --> 00:47:29,708
I felt the same at first.

693
00:47:29,709 --> 00:47:32,249
I know how it feels. I was like you.

694
00:47:32,250 --> 00:47:33,833
He stole my lines.

695
00:47:33,834 --> 00:47:36,625
But real growth begins

696
00:47:36,626 --> 00:47:39,374
the moment you admit your limitations.

697
00:47:39,375 --> 00:47:41,291
Remember that feeling.

698
00:47:41,292 --> 00:47:44,041
- Let's call it a day.
- No.

699
00:47:44,042 --> 00:47:45,918
I'm not done.

700
00:47:56,292 --> 00:47:57,959
What are you doing?

701
00:48:00,334 --> 00:48:01,959
What?

702
00:48:07,709 --> 00:48:10,792
I mean, why are you...

703
00:48:16,042 --> 00:48:17,709
Let's go.

704
00:48:32,334 --> 00:48:34,374
What?

705
00:48:34,375 --> 00:48:36,291
Why did you suddenly take your clothes off?

706
00:48:36,292 --> 00:48:38,708
Train as if it's a real fight.

707
00:48:38,709 --> 00:48:41,166
Who knows?

708
00:48:41,167 --> 00:48:43,626
Suspects may attack you like this.

709
00:48:45,000 --> 00:48:47,374
Wow, Ji Dae Se.

710
00:48:47,375 --> 00:48:48,625
He's crazier than I thought.

711
00:48:48,626 --> 00:48:51,166
He looks good, though.

712
00:48:51,167 --> 00:48:53,000
What, his body?

713
00:48:53,626 --> 00:48:55,082
No, I mean his energy.

714
00:48:55,083 --> 00:48:57,249
- Nah, it's the body.
- No, it's the energy.

715
00:48:57,250 --> 00:49:00,334
Inspector Cha has met his match.

716
00:49:08,792 --> 00:49:11,041
The technology we create

717
00:49:11,042 --> 00:49:14,374
must not be something we bet on.

718
00:49:14,375 --> 00:49:16,791
When we treat human lives as numbers

719
00:49:16,792 --> 00:49:20,249
in order to bring profits to investors,

720
00:49:20,250 --> 00:49:24,833
such technology is no longer 'smart.'

721
00:49:24,834 --> 00:49:27,208
Chimera's mission is to create

722
00:49:27,209 --> 00:49:32,750
technologies that protect humans,
not defeat them.

723
00:49:32,751 --> 00:49:36,374
I will carry the mission forward,

724
00:49:36,375 --> 00:49:41,625
and ask myself this question
over and over again,

725
00:49:41,626 --> 00:49:44,042
what should technology exist for?

726
00:49:49,834 --> 00:49:52,834
- I'm so moved, she spoke so well.
- Right?

727
00:49:52,835 --> 00:49:55,999
Not a trace of her usual clumsy self.

728
00:49:56,000 --> 00:49:59,374
It feels like Tesla ten years ago.

729
00:49:59,375 --> 00:50:01,750
Gotta buy shares when they go public.

730
00:50:01,751 --> 00:50:03,416
Can't we like, use our acquaintance

731
00:50:03,417 --> 00:50:06,041
- to get some of the shares first?
- No.

732
00:50:06,042 --> 00:50:09,042
They won't go public for a while.

733
00:50:25,292 --> 00:50:28,541
I think I can understand

734
00:50:28,542 --> 00:50:31,500
why Dr. Baek did what he did.

735
00:50:32,626 --> 00:50:36,249
He created the technology
to make the world a better place.

736
00:50:36,250 --> 00:50:39,791
He dreaded the possibility
that it might be used to kill people.

737
00:50:39,792 --> 00:50:42,208
He endured pressure from investors,

738
00:50:42,209 --> 00:50:46,082
and the constant demand to ignore ethics.

739
00:50:46,083 --> 00:50:49,417
He stood his ground without any complaints.

740
00:50:50,751 --> 00:50:53,792
But he must have felt that everyone,

741
00:50:54,334 --> 00:50:56,958
including his own wife,

742
00:50:56,959 --> 00:50:59,625
denied what he stood for.

743
00:50:59,626 --> 00:51:01,750
I think that despair,

744
00:51:01,751 --> 00:51:03,458
that utter loneliness,

745
00:51:03,459 --> 00:51:07,334
ultimately led him to taking his own life.

746
00:51:08,918 --> 00:51:11,166
He must've felt lonely.

747
00:51:11,167 --> 00:51:13,416
He's drowning, fighting for breath,

748
00:51:13,417 --> 00:51:15,666
while everyone around him

749
00:51:15,667 --> 00:51:18,667
is waiting for him to sink quietly.

750
00:51:20,584 --> 00:51:22,542
I should have done more.

751
00:51:23,167 --> 00:51:24,499
If I'd stood by him,

752
00:51:24,500 --> 00:51:27,751
- and supported him more-
- It starts today.

753
00:51:29,584 --> 00:51:32,125
The burden Dr. Baek used to carry,

754
00:51:32,751 --> 00:51:34,626
now they are on your shoulders.

755
00:51:52,709 --> 00:51:55,541
Where's everybody? The office is empty.

756
00:51:55,542 --> 00:51:57,374
They're out on the field.

757
00:51:57,375 --> 00:52:00,166
- Can I help you?
- No need.

758
00:52:00,167 --> 00:52:02,375
I just brought some documents.

759
00:52:10,042 --> 00:52:11,958
They're on your desk.

760
00:52:11,959 --> 00:52:14,584
It's from NFS.

761
00:52:17,459 --> 00:52:19,209
NFS?

762
00:52:29,542 --> 00:52:32,125
[NFS]

763
00:52:39,375 --> 00:52:41,709
[DNA Test Report]

764
00:52:45,042 --> 00:52:48,291
<i>Hit-and-run on Yulmok Hill.</i>

765
00:52:48,292 --> 00:52:51,709
<i>Hubby, when will you get home?</i>

766
00:52:57,417 --> 00:52:59,875
<i>Previous analysis results,</i>

767
00:52:59,876 --> 00:53:02,292
<i>DNA amplification failed.</i>

768
00:53:04,292 --> 00:53:07,918
[DNA Analysis Results]

769
00:53:10,375 --> 00:53:13,125
[STR Profiling Successful]

770
00:53:17,000 --> 00:53:20,374
<i>The profile is ready for cross-checking</i>

771
00:53:20,375 --> 00:53:22,499
<i>with the NFS DNA database.</i>

772
00:53:22,500 --> 00:53:24,999
[Test Requested By TCI]

773
00:53:25,000 --> 00:53:27,209
[Point Of Contact: Cha Yeon Ho]

774
00:53:32,167 --> 00:53:33,584
Cha Yeon Ho.

775
00:53:51,375 --> 00:53:54,792
ID and visitation request form, please.

776
00:54:21,918 --> 00:54:25,791
You keep coming here
and asking the same questions.

777
00:54:25,792 --> 00:54:27,625
But my answer won't change.

778
00:54:27,626 --> 00:54:30,875
I met her.

779
00:54:30,876 --> 00:54:32,626
The cop?

780
00:54:34,876 --> 00:54:36,041
What did she say?

781
00:54:36,042 --> 00:54:39,500
She doesn't know who I really am.

782
00:54:43,667 --> 00:54:45,041
- We're back!
- We're back!

783
00:54:45,042 --> 00:54:47,041
Captain! Yoon Ji Yoon was so cool!

784
00:54:47,042 --> 00:54:50,249
I guess position does make the person.

785
00:54:50,250 --> 00:54:52,918
Investigator Cha, let's talk.

786
00:55:09,083 --> 00:55:10,958
[DNA Test Report]

787
00:55:10,959 --> 00:55:12,999
- DNA test-
- How dare you?

788
00:55:13,000 --> 00:55:14,751
You thought you can...

789
00:55:15,667 --> 00:55:20,375
Dig around my wife's case behind my back?

790
00:55:21,876 --> 00:55:25,167
I apologize for requesting the test
without telling you first.

791
00:55:26,375 --> 00:55:28,541
I heard from NFS,

792
00:55:28,542 --> 00:55:31,875
that you were demoted while working on my case,

793
00:55:31,876 --> 00:55:34,375
and your wife had an accident afterwards.

794
00:55:36,834 --> 00:55:38,208
Maybe I am to blame.

795
00:55:38,209 --> 00:55:39,833
Don't get ahead of yourself.

796
00:55:39,834 --> 00:55:42,583
This has got nothing to do with you.

797
00:55:42,584 --> 00:55:47,542
It's not something you can use
to relieve your sense of guilt.

798
00:55:49,626 --> 00:55:51,375
Stop pursuing the case.

799
00:55:52,125 --> 00:55:54,125
What are you afraid of?

800
00:55:56,417 --> 00:55:59,750
Reliving a past trauma
just to not have any closure?

801
00:55:59,751 --> 00:56:01,374
Or,

802
00:56:01,375 --> 00:56:05,209
are you afraid to face that painful memory?

803
00:56:06,667 --> 00:56:08,333
Then why are you

804
00:56:08,334 --> 00:56:11,250
asking about the accident
every time you visit NFS?

805
00:56:13,167 --> 00:56:15,959
The statute of limitations
will expire in a month.

806
00:56:17,209 --> 00:56:19,209
It may be your last chance.

807
00:56:20,584 --> 00:56:23,334
At least check the DNA database.

808
00:56:52,709 --> 00:56:55,751
[Park Hae Ok, mother of Ji Dae Se]

809
00:56:57,334 --> 00:56:59,249
Mom,

810
00:56:59,250 --> 00:57:00,918
how are you doing?

811
00:57:04,083 --> 00:57:06,375
Mom, you once said,

812
00:57:06,959 --> 00:57:09,334
catching bad guys is easy,

813
00:57:10,167 --> 00:57:12,417
compared to not hating people.

814
00:57:15,209 --> 00:57:16,918
And I...

815
00:57:19,876 --> 00:57:22,334
It's really not easy for me.

816
00:57:28,792 --> 00:57:30,918
I'll get to the bottom of it.

817
00:57:32,375 --> 00:57:34,626
I promise.

818
00:58:21,792 --> 00:58:23,833
- Hey!
- Make a wish.

819
00:58:23,834 --> 00:58:25,958
So we can be together for the birthday party.

820
00:58:25,959 --> 00:58:27,583
What is it?

821
00:58:27,584 --> 00:58:30,542
I'm good. Enjoy the cake.

822
00:58:31,876 --> 00:58:33,249
Was she hit?

823
00:58:33,250 --> 00:58:36,291
- I think she's hurt!
- Will the baby okay?

824
00:58:36,292 --> 00:58:37,583
She pushed me!

825
00:58:37,584 --> 00:58:39,541
A friend would not force him

826
00:58:39,542 --> 00:58:41,374
to purchase a life insurance.

827
00:58:41,375 --> 00:58:42,291
A cop?

828
00:58:42,292 --> 00:58:44,625
There's a man down in the tunnel.

829
00:58:44,626 --> 00:58:46,584
Brake, brake!

830
00:58:47,626 --> 00:58:48,792
Shut your mouth!

831
00:58:51,459 --> 00:58:53,667
[People Of The Police Station]

832
00:59:00,751 --> 00:59:02,958
Cars these days are really smart.

833
00:59:02,959 --> 00:59:06,249
They adjust speed and find lanes on their own.

834
00:59:06,250 --> 00:59:08,166
They even help you brake.

835
00:59:08,167 --> 00:59:10,708
It feels like they can do everything.

836
00:59:10,709 --> 00:59:13,958
But don't be mistaken.

837
00:59:13,959 --> 00:59:17,791
They can help you drive,
but they can't drive for you.

838
00:59:17,792 --> 00:59:20,208
Think of training wheels.

839
00:59:20,209 --> 00:59:22,709
You can't let go of the handle.

840
00:59:23,584 --> 00:59:27,750
The system may not recognize
sudden cut-ins or stops.

841
00:59:27,751 --> 00:59:29,750
In fact, death toll from expressway accidents

842
00:59:29,751 --> 00:59:32,416
increased by more than 50% this year.

843
00:59:32,417 --> 00:59:36,750
The police attributed it to people's
overconfidence in driving assistance.

844
00:59:36,751 --> 00:59:39,041
It is the same for DUI.

845
00:59:39,042 --> 00:59:41,208
Even if auto drive was on,

846
00:59:41,209 --> 00:59:43,918
you may be held responsible
in case of an accident.

847
00:59:44,959 --> 00:59:48,333
And you may have wondered
while watching the show,

848
00:59:48,334 --> 00:59:50,875
is it really possible to hack a car?

849
00:59:50,876 --> 00:59:52,999
Yes, they can.

850
00:59:53,000 --> 00:59:56,458
As early as ten years ago,
someone hacked into moving cars,

851
00:59:56,459 --> 00:59:59,291
resulting in recalls of 1.4 million vehicles.

852
00:59:59,292 --> 01:00:01,082
Today,

853
01:00:01,083 --> 01:00:02,666
you can use apps

854
01:00:02,667 --> 01:00:05,791
to open doors and start the engine.

855
01:00:05,792 --> 01:00:08,166
The number of security breaches
targeting these technologies

856
01:00:08,167 --> 01:00:10,833
has exceeded 400 per year.

857
01:00:10,834 --> 01:00:15,374
And most of them were attacked remotely.

858
01:00:15,375 --> 01:00:18,374
Remember two things.

859
01:00:18,375 --> 01:00:20,666
Update your software in time,

860
01:00:20,667 --> 01:00:23,541
and don't connect devices
that you don't know about.

861
01:00:23,542 --> 01:00:25,583
Someone may hack into your car,

862
01:00:25,584 --> 01:00:27,875
to steal it or take control.

863
01:00:27,876 --> 01:00:30,875
Convenience is one thing, security is another.

864
01:00:30,876 --> 01:00:33,374
Security is your responsibility. Stay vigilant.

865
01:00:33,375 --> 01:00:35,541
Remember. It's you sitting behind the wheel,

866
01:00:35,542 --> 01:00:37,917
Not the car itself.
